# 🖥️ Day 1 Hacker Startup Script

A beginner-friendly Python script that simulates the startup sequence of a "hacking tool" — printing operator info, target details, and a ready status in a stylized terminal format. Great as a first step into learning Python basics like variables and `print()` formatting.

> ⚠️ **Disclaimer:** This is an educational/fun project only. It does not perform any real network scanning, hacking, or exploitation. All values (target IP, port, etc.) are placeholders for learning purposes.

---

## 📋 Features

- Stylized "hacker-style" welcome banner
- Displays operator (hacker) name
- Displays target system IP and port
- Simple, beginner-friendly Python code structure

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.x installed on your machine

### Installation
```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/day1-hacker-startup-script.git
cd day1-hacker-startup-script
```

### Run the Script
```bash
python3 hacker_script.py
```

